Five Chain-of-Density iterations ran, each holding roughly 60 words while folding in entities the previous pass lacked: iteration 2 added the `--only` rule, blanket staging, and sibling sessions' work-in-progress; iteration 3 added `git show --stat HEAD`, scratch files, and the fresh-import exception; iteration 4 added the `-u`/`.` variants, per-file claiming, and reverting pushed commits; iteration 5 added "whole files, nothing else", the before-building trigger, and "session's own". The final pass compressed the ~110-word source to 63 words with every command, check, and exception intact.

<RESULT>
Office shared-checkout rule: commit with --only, staging conversation-touched whole files, nothing else. Blanket staging (git add -A/--all/-u/., commit -a) sweeps sibling sessions' work-in-progress and scratch files. Before building on it, list staged files (git status, git show --stat HEAD), claiming each as this session's own; otherwise unstage, amend, or revert already-pushed commits. User-ordered sweeps or fresh wholly-yours imports: carry on.
</RESULT>
